      "sourceFolder": "content",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Phase 3A Character Forge\ntype: handbook\ncategory: Gameplay Architecture\ntags:\n  - gameplay\n  - character-forge\n  - phase-3a\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Phase 3A Character Forge\n\n## Overview\nCharacter Forge replaces the old creator label and becomes the guided character build foundation for Asteria.\n\n## Forge Flow\n1. Race\n2. Class\n3. Appearance\n4. Origin\n5. Characteristics\n6. Skills\n7. Equipment\n8. Review\n\n## Rules\nClass talents are displayed from class progression data and are not freely selected during the forge flow.\n\nProfession slots start as \"No Profession Learned\" and remain campaign-earned.\n\nStarting skill selection requires exactly 4 skills from the Skill Compendium.\n\n## Compatibility\nThe older internal create-character route remains as a compatibility alias so existing dashboard buttons, saves, and account routes open Character Forge instead of breaking.\n",
      "body": "# Phase 3A Character Forge\n\n## Overview\nCharacter Forge replaces the old creator label and becomes the guided character build foundation for Asteria.\n\n## Forge Flow\n1. Race\n2. Class\n3. Appearance\n4. Origin\n5. Characteristics\n6. Skills\n7. Equipment\n8. Review\n\n## Rules\nClass talents are displayed from class progression data and are not freely selected during the forge flow.\n\nProfession slots start as \"No Profession Learned\" and remain campaign-earned.\n\nStarting skill selection requires exactly 4 skills from the Skill Compendium.\n\n## Compatibility\nThe older internal create-character route remains as a compatibility alias so existing dashboard buttons, saves, and account routes open Character Forge instead of breaking.",
