      "content": "---\ntitle: \"Tempestborn Undien\"\nslug: \"tempestborn-undien\"\ntype: race\nraceCategory: \"Demi Races\"\nsecondaryCategory: \"Undien Races\"\ntertiaryCategory: \nplayable: true\nsize: \nmovement: \"9m\"\nlanguages: []\nmagicAffinity:\n  - \"Storm\"\n  - \"Lightning\"\n  - \"Water\"\nessenceAffinity: []\ntags:\n  - \"race\"\n  - \"demi-races\"\n  - \"undien-races\"\nimages:\n  male: \"assets/races/tempestborn-undien/tempestborn-undien-male-adult.png\"\n  female: \"assets/races/tempestborn-undien/tempestborn-undien-female-adult.png\"\nvisibility: public\nsourceOrder: 182\n---\n\n# Tempestborn Undien\n\n## Overview\n- Race Category: Demi-Race\n- Race Type: Spiritborn Humanoid\n- Parent Race: Tempest Spirit × Humanoid\n- Playable: Yes\n- Rarity: Rare\n\n## Racial Features\n- Height Range:\n  - Male: 175cm - 205cm\n  - Female: 165cm - 195cm\n\n- Weight Range:\n  - 65kg - 110kg\n\n- Skin:\n  - Smooth skin infused with storm mana\n  - Faint electrical energy may dance across the body during heightened emotions\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Storm Grey\n    - Slate Blue\n    - Silver Grey\n    - Pale Blue\n    - Thundercloud Black\n\n- Hair:\n  - Constantly appears windswept\n  - Often crackles with static electricity\n  - Colour Range:\n    - White\n    - Silver\n    - Blue\n    - Black\n    - Dark Grey\n\n- Eyes:\n  - Bright and luminous\n  - Often glow during storms\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Electric Blue\n    - Silver\n    - White\n    - Violet\n    - Golden Yellow\n\n- Hands:\n  - Long dexterous fingers\n  - Often emit tiny static discharges\n\n- Face:\n  - Sharp features\n  - Intense expressions\n  - Highly expressive eyes\n\n- Ears:\n  - Slightly elongated\n  - Wind-shaped fin ridges\n\n- Markings:\n  - Lightning-like bioluminescent patterns\n  - Glow brightly during spellcasting\n  - Most commonly appear along arms, neck, chest, and face\n\n- Body:\n  - Lean athletic build\n  - Fast reflexes\n  - Constant subtle movement even when standing still\n\n---\n\n## Racial Characteristics\n| Characteristic | Buff/Debuff | Stat Rolls | Characteristics Tier Cap |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------ |\n| Strength       | +2          | 4d6        | Tier 3                   |\n| Dexterity      | 0           | 3d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Agility        | 0           | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Constitution   | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Endurance      | +2          | 4d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Intelligence   | -2          | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Wisdom         | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Charisma       | +1          | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Luck           | 0           | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n\n---\n\n## Racial Traits\n### Storm Sense\n\n#### Description\nTempestborn possess an innate awareness of atmospheric conditions and storm currents. The winds themselves whisper warnings to them.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Gain +2 Perception during storms, rainfall, or high winds.\n- Can sense approaching storms up to 24 hours in advance.\n- Detect major weather changes several hours before they occur.\n- Gain advantage on Survival checks involving weather prediction.\n\n---\n\n### Child of the Tempest\n\n#### Description\nStorm mana flows naturally through the body of a Tempestborn, empowering their lightning and wind abilities.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Lightning and Storm spells cost 10% less Mana.\n- Gain +1 to Lightning and Storm spell rolls.\n- Resistant to Lightning damage.\n- Gain advantage on rolls against natural weather hazards.\n\n---\n\n### Lightning Reflexes\n\n#### Description\nThe speed of the storm is reflected in every movement a Tempestborn makes.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Gain +2 Initiative.\n- Gain +1 Agility.\n- Gain advantage on reaction-based checks.\n- Reduce fall damage by 50%.\n\n---\n\n### Breath of the Storm\n\n#### Description\nLike all Undien, Tempestborn are equally at home above and below the water. Their storm-touched nature allows them to move effortlessly through rain, wind, and sea.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Can breathe underwater indefinitely.\n- Ignore underwater combat penalties.\n- Swim speed is doubled.\n- Ignore movement penalties caused by heavy rain, strong winds, or rough seas.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Culture\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Historical Figures\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Settlements\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Relations\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Traits & Biology\n- Swim Speed: 18m\n- Ignore difficult terrain caused by storms and heavy rain.\n- Gain +3m movement speed during storms.\n- Suffer no penalties from strong winds.\n- Can maintain balance on unstable surfaces during severe weather.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Bonuses\n- Enhanced Storm Magic\n- Enhanced Lightning Magic\n- Exceptional Mobility\n- Superior Reflexes\n- Advanced Weather Awareness\n\n### ⚠️ Drawbacks\n- Emotionally volatile during intense storms.\n- Lightning-based magical overload can occur during extreme mana usage.\n- Less tolerant of enclosed underground environments.\n- Often struggle with patience and long periods of inactivity.\n\n---\n\n## Gallery\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## GM Notes\nGM-only information coming soon.\n",
